    <briefdescription>
<para>The &quot;Elvis&quot; expression, which is used to optionally substitute the value of the second expression iff the value of the first expression is null. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Experimental feature: Alternatively, this expression tests a &quot;conditional&quot; first expression (one that yields both a Boolean and at least one additional value), and substitutes the value of the second expression iff that first Boolean value yielded is False, and otherwise yields the second value from the first expression.</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para><computeroutput>COND_ELSE: &quot;?:&quot;</computeroutput> - the &quot;elvis&quot; operator </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
